  "failure": {
    "body": "#### Description\n\nI set up a fresh Debian 10 (buster) instance on Amazon EC2. After installing docker and installing the prerequisites, python, pip, jinja2 and j2cli and adding the user to the docker group, I encounter an error when running make all.\n\n#### Steps to reproduce the issue:\n1. Stand up a fresh Debian 10 instance (in my case on EC2)\n2. sudo modprobe overlay\n3. Install docker\n4. Add user to docker group using sudo gpasswd -a ${USER} docker\n5. git clone https://github.com/Azure/sonic-buildimage.git\n6. make init\n7. make configure PLATFORM=broadcom\n8. make all\n\n#### Describe the results you received:\n\nEach test failed with this error:\n\nname = 'eeprom'\n\ndef isModuleLoaded(name):\n with open('/proc/modules') as f:\nE IOError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: '/proc/modules'\n\n#### Describe the results you expected:\n\n#### Output of `show version`:\n\n```\n(paste your output here)\n```\n#### Output of `show techsupport`:\n\n```\n(paste your output here or download and attach the file here )\n```\n\n#### Additional information you deem important (e.g. issue happens only occasionally):"
  },
  "resolution": {
    "pr_number": 7527,
    "repository": "sonic-net/sonic-buildimage",
    "url": "https://github.com/sonic-net/sonic-buildimage/pull/7527",
    "title": "[Arista] Update platform configurations and library",
    "merged_at": "2021-05-06T17:59:22Z",
    "description": "Platform library changes\n - Fix the use of /proc/modules during testing, fixes #7463\n - Add `libsfp-eeprom.so` build to read/write xcvr eeproms in C\n - Add some more reboot-cause information\n - Write down temperature hw thresholds to the sensors\n - Report software thresholds through platform api\n - Writ `port_name sysfs` file of optoe`\n - Tests enhancements\n - Fix dependency issues for chassis provisioning\n\nPlatform configuration changes\n - Add `pcie.yaml` configuration for a few platforms\n - Mount `libsfp-eeprom.so` inside `pmon`\n - Fix `Arista-7050SX3-48C8` and `Arista-7050SX3-48YC8' platform and hwsku\n - Miscellaneous fixes",
